          "buttonOnMobile": false,
          "label": "<p>A medical officer in a low-transmission state is preparing the district malaria </p>",
          "x": 30,
          "y": 30,
          "width": 40,
          "height": 25,
          "libraryTitle": "Multiple Choice",
          "action": {
            "library": "H5P.MultiChoice 1.16",
            "params": {
              "question": "<p>A medical officer in a low-transmission state is preparing the district malaria elimination plan in 2026. Under the NFME 2016–2030, by which year should the district target zero indigenous malaria cases?</p>",
              "answers": [
                {
                  "text": "<div>2025</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Incorrect. 2025 is not a specified milestone under the NFME. The framework sets differentiated targets: 2027 for low-transmission states and 2030 for nationwide elimination.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>2027</div>",
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Correct. The NFME targets zero indigenous malaria cases by 2027 specifically in low-transmission states, with nationwide elimination by 2030. Strategies include universal RDT access, ACT, and ITN/LLIN distribution.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>2030</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Incorrect. While 2030 is the nationwide elimination target, low-transmission states have the earlier target of 2027. A medical officer in such a state should plan for the 2027 deadline.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>2035</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>Incorrect. The NFME 2016–2030 sets 2030 as its outermost deadline (nationwide). Low-transmission states must achieve elimination by 2027, three years earlier.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                }
              ],
              "overallFeedback": [
                {
                  "from": 0,
                  "to": 50,
                  "feedback": "The NFME uses a phased approach: low-transmission states → 2027; nationwide → 2030. This differentiation is key to India's malaria elimination strategy."
                },
                {
                  "from": 51,
                  "to": 100,
                  "feedback": "Correct! Differentiated targets allow focused resource allocation — low-transmission states (API <1) push for elimination first, building momentum toward the 2030 nationwide target."
                }
              ],
              "behaviour": {
